"""JVS25V100M6X4 - 100 uF 25 V 20 % SMD aluminium electrolytic capacitor, D6.3 x 4.5 mm. Bare part.

Datasheet: JIERR JVS series aluminium electrolytic capacitors (LCSC C51953404), pages 1-2.

Ratings (page 1, specifications): operating temperature -55 to +105 C; capacitance
tolerance +-20 % (120 Hz, 20 C); leakage I <= 0.01 CV or 3 uA, whichever is greater (25 uA
here) after 2 minutes at rated voltage; tan delta <= 0.18 at 120 Hz for 25 V (ESR about
2.4 Ohm at 120 Hz from tan delta / (2 pi f C); no 100 kHz ESR is given); endurance 1000 h
at 105 C. Part number (page 2): JVS series, 25 V, 100 uF, M = +-20 %, 6X4 case. Case
D6.3 x L4.5 mm, base 6.6 x 6.6 mm, land spacing 7.3 mm (page 2 dimension table, D = 6.3,
L = 4.5 row). Ripple current: 54 mA at 120 Hz per the LCSC listing; the page 2 ripple table
did not extract to text (TODO: confirm against the PDF).

Polarity: pin 1 (POS) is the + terminal, on the chamfered side of the footprint, which is
also marked "+" on the silkscreen. The package warns when the voltage across POS and NEG
exceeds the 25 V rating.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Capacitance", "Voltage")
load("@stdlib/utils.zen", "format_value")

POS = io(Net)
NEG = io(Net)

capacitance = Capacitance("100uF 20%")
voltage = Voltage("25V")

if POS.voltage and NEG.voltage and voltage < POS.voltage.diff(NEG.voltage):
    warn(
        f"JVS25V100M6X4 rated {voltage} is below the voltage across it ({POS.voltage.diff(NEG.voltage)})",
        kind="capacitor.voltage_rating",
    )

Component(
    name="JVS25V100M6X4",
    prefix="C",
    symbol=Symbol(library="JVS25V100M6X4.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("CAP-SMD_BD6.3-L6.6-W6.6-LS7.3-FD_JVS25V100M6X4.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="JVS25V100M6X4", manufacturer="JIERR"),
    pins={"+": POS, "-": NEG},
    properties={
        "value": format_value(capacitance, voltage),
        "capacitance": capacitance,
        "voltage": voltage,
    },
    type="capacitor",
)
